# sbase: suckless.org's POSIX utilities, in the boot image (usr/bin/<tool>)
# so the shell has them before /data is there. third_party/sbase is the
# tree of commit c546c3a5724c81cee9a11d816a38ccdf17472129 (2026-05-22),
# nothing changed: sbase has no releases, so the version is the date.
#
# What is built: sbase's own Makefile builds libutf.a and libutil.a and
# each tool from <tool>.c and the two libraries, and so does build.sh
# (its flags, no -DPREFIX: nothing here installs). Three tools fork
# (find -exec, time, xargs) and run ours (OVERRIDES). What is left out,
# and why, is in docs/M13-PLAN.md's "P1 notes".
#
# One program per list, not per tool (upstream's own "sbase-box": each
# tool's main renamed <tool>_main and a table that picks one by the name
# the program was started as). A static POSIX program is about 250 KB of C
# library and runtime whatever it does, so 80 programs would be 20 MB of
# boot image, which `update` has a limit on (UPDATE_FILE_MAX). The three
# programs are the three lists below; each tool is a `multicall` name of
# the one that holds it (the boot image names a box once for every tool in
# it: tools/mkbootfs.py stores identical files once), and the shell starts
# a program under its bootfs name, so the tool is the basename of argv[0].
# `usr/bin/sbase-<list> <tool> args` works too.
#
# The lists are the least each tool needs (/esp, the boot stick's loader
# and kernel, is never in them):
#   sbase-plain   a terminal and pipes only: filters of their input (tr,
#                 seq, printf, ...) and things that report (uname)
#   sbase-ro      files read: /data, other sticks, and /boot
#   sbase-rw      files read and written (cp, rm, sort -o, sed w, ...), and
#                 the programs that start others (find -exec, xargs, env,
#                 time): a child gets its parent's namespace, so these hold
#                 what the commands they run may need
name        sbase
version     20260522
revision    1
summary     suckless.org's POSIX utilities (ls, cp, sed, ...) in three multi-call programs
homepage    https://core.suckless.org/sbase/
category    base
licence     MIT
licence-file LICENSE
vendored    sbase
place       boot
style       custom
program     bin/sbase-plain
program     bin/sbase-ro
program     bin/sbase-rw
multicall   bin/sbase-plain basename dirname echo false true yes seq printf sleep printenv
multicall   bin/sbase-plain tr uname whoami logname hostname pwd tty date expr cal
multicall   bin/sbase-ro cat cmp comm cut du expand fold grep head join ls md5sum nl od paste
multicall   bin/sbase-ro sha1sum sha256sum sha512sum tail test uniq unexpand wc which cksum
multicall   bin/sbase-ro cols dc pathchk strings tsort uuencode
multicall   bin/sbase-rw cp mv rm rmdir mkdir touch tee split dd tar ed sed sort find xargs
multicall   bin/sbase-rw env time uudecode unlink
cpe         cpe:2.3:a:suckless:sbase
